---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {countries} from '../../lib/resume';
---
<Layout title="Resume & CV Guides by Country" active="guides"><main id="main" class="content-page"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CLARITY FOR YOUR NEXT MOVE</span><h1>Your experience travels.<br/>Make your CV travel with it.</h1><p>Practical starting points for applying in five destinations. Adapt your resume to the employer, the role, and the instructions in the vacancy.</p></div><div class="country-grid">{countries.map(c=><a href={`/countries/${c.slug}/`} class="country-card"><span class="country-code">{c.code}</span><h2>{c.name}</h2><p>{c.tip}</p><span class="read-more">Read the guide →</span></a>)}<a href="/guides/ats-friendly-resume/" class="country-card"><span class="country-code">ATS</span><h2>Make your resume easy to read</h2><p>Understand clear formatting, text extraction and the difference between readability and job matching.</p><span class="read-more">Read the guide →</span></a></div><div class="article-note"><h2 style="font-size:21px">Already have a CV?</h2><p>Learn what importing can recover, what you should check, and how to refresh your old document.</p><a href="/guides/import-existing-cv/" class="button secondary">A guide to importing your CV →</a></div></main></Layout>
